#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:18
msgid "Firmware on the Wireless Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:20
msgid "The kit has been shipped in two versions. Which one you have decides whether there is anything to flash at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:25
msgid "ESPC2-01 (current version)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:27
msgid "**There is nothing to flash.** The module leaves the factory with the ESP-AT firmware already burned, and the kit's sketches only send it AT commands. This chapter is here so you can *check* the module, not so you can reprogram it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:31
msgid "**1. Check the version**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:33
msgid "Wire the module as in :ref:`c201_connect_blynk`, open the **Serial Monitor** at **115200**, set the line ending to **Both NL & CR** (or send with Enter) and type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:40
msgid "A healthy module answers with four lines and ``OK``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:52
msgid "The line that tells you this is **our** build is ``compile time(7c092f9)...``. ``Bin version:v4.1.1.0(ESP32C2-2MB-BLE)`` is printed by the official Bluetooth-only build as well, so it is not proof on its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:56
msgid "**2. Check that the Wi-Fi part is really included**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:62
msgid "The answer must be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:69
msgid "An ``ERROR`` instead of ``+CWMODE:1`` means the module carries a Bluetooth-only firmware, so the Wi-Fi projects of this kit cannot work with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:72
msgid "**3. If the module does not answer at all**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:74
msgid "Go through these in order - nearly every case is one of them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:76
msgid "the adapter is powered from **5 V**, not 3.3 V;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:77
msgid "the external power supply (9-12 V) is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima - on USB alone the module browns out while its radio starts;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:79
msgid "TX of the module goes to RX of the board and RX to TX;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:80
msgid "IO9 is left **floating** (do not pull it low - that is download mode);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:81
msgid "press the reset button on the board and try ``AT`` again after about two seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:83
msgid "**4. If the firmware is the wrong one**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/burn_firmware.rst:85
msgid "This cannot be repaired in the field: the module has to be taken out of the adapter, put into download mode and flashed with the matching ESP-AT build. Please send the ``AT+GMR`` output to **service@sunfounder.com** and we will replace the module."
msgstr ""

